  <section id="sol-b2b" class="section wrap feature" aria-labelledby="fb-title">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <p class="kicker">B2B Commerce</p>
      <h2 id="fb-title">Sell to businesses with negotiated, tiered pricing</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Pricing resolves by who is buying and how many. Customer groups share a
        price list, quantity breaks apply within it, and the cart enforces the
        same one-price-at-a-time rule it already uses for everyone else — so a
        wholesale account and a walk-in shopper hit the same checkout.
      </p>
      <ul class="tick">
        <li>Customer groups, each mapped to a price list</li>
        <li>Quantity breaks resolved per line, not per cart</li>
        <li>Money stored as integer minor units — no rounding drift on volume orders</li>
        <li>Scoped API keys, so a buyer's procurement system can order without a login</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/gocommerce/#use-cases" data-ev="gocommerce_explore">How B2B pricing resolves</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/gocommerce/#modules">Payments and invoicing modules</a>
      </div>
      <p class="sol-prim">core/pricing.go — customer groups, price lists, quantity pricing</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="feature-visual flow" aria-labelledby="fb-cap">
      <figcaption id="fb-cap" class="flow-cap">How a B2B price is found</figcaption>
      <div class="arch-row"><h3>Customer</h3><p>in group: wholesale</p></div>
      <p class="arch-wire"><span>group → price list</span></p>
      <div class="arch-row arch-engine"><h3>Price list</h3><p>wholesale-2026</p></div>
      <p class="arch-wire"><span>quantity 250 → break</span></p>
      <div class="arch-row arch-store"><h3>Unit price</h3><p>resolved once, per line</p></div>
      <p class="arch-wire"><span>same rule as retail</span></p>
      <div class="arch-row arch-data"><h3>Cart</h3><p>integer minor units</p></div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="solutions" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="sol-title">
    <h2 id="sol-title">And the other two shapes of store</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Engine capabilities, not customer stories. Each names the primitive that
      does the work, so the claim can be checked in the source.
    </p>

    <div class="solutions">
      <article class="solution" id="sol-d2c">
        <svg class="sol-ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-bag"/></svg>
        <h3>Run a direct-to-consumer store</h3>
        <p>The default. Guest checkout, cash on delivery and manual fulfillment are built in, so a store sells with no modules installed at all. Add Stripe or a carrier when you need them, not before.</p>
        <p class="sol-prim">Carts, checkout, orders, inventory</p>
        <a href="/gocommerce/#quickstart" data-ev="quickstart_click">Start with the default store</a>
      </article>
      <article class="solution" id="sol-channels">
        <svg class="sol-ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-server"/></svg>
        <h3>Serve several storefronts from one catalogue</h3>
        <p>Channels are storefronts over one catalogue, differing in what is published to each. A store that never creates a second channel pays nothing for the feature.</p>
        <p class="sol-prim">Channels, per-channel publishing</p>
        <a href="/gocommerce/#use-cases" data-ev="gocommerce_explore">How channels are scoped</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

